==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ru|годъ}} {{ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|ru|gʰedʰ}}
From {{inh|ru|orv|годъ||time, period, year, age}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*godъ||suitable time}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*gʰodʰo-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-||to unite, be associated, be suitable}}

Cognates include
{{cog|uk|годi||enough}},
{{cog|bg|годе||[[ever]]}} (as in {{l|bg|кой-годе}} = whoever),
{{cog|cs|hod}},
{{cog|pl|gody||yearly feast}},
{{cog|hsb|hody||Christmas}},
{{cog|dsb|gódy||Christmas}},
{{cog|lv|gadigs}},
{{cog|de|Gatte||husband}}, {{m|de|gätlich||convenient}},
{{cog|nl|gegade}}, {{m|nl|gade}}, {{m|nl|gading}},
as well as {{cog|en|gather}}, {{m|en|good}},
{{cog|nl|gader}}, {{m|nl|goed}},
and {{cog|de|gut}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|Ru-год.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}
* {{homophones|гот|lang=ru}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|e|or|c||(1)|or|c||(1)(2)|лет|par=+|loc=в +}}

# [[year]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[из го́да в год]]|year in and year out, from year to year}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[в]] [[этот|э́том]] '''году́'''|this year}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[года́ми]]|for years; for years on end}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[девяностый|девяно́стые]] '''го́ды'''|the '90s}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[уче́бный]] '''год'''|school year; academic year}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[новый|Но́вый]] год|New Year’s Day}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[два́дцать оди́н]] год.|He is 21 years old.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[два́дцать три]] го́да.|He is 23 years old.''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[он|Ему́]] [[два́дцать пять]] [[лето|лет]].|He is 25 years old.''}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[ты́сяча]] [[девятьсо́т]] [[девяно́сто]] [[второ́й]] год|(year) 1992 (''in words'')}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[две]] [[тысяча|ты́сячи]] [[оди́ннадцатый]] год|(year) 2011 (''in words'')}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[с]] [[каждый|ка́ждым]] '''го́дом'''|from year to year, year by year, year after year}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[по]] [[сравнение|сравне́нию]] [[с]] [[тот же|те́м же]] [[период|пери́одом]] [[прошлый|про́шлого]] '''го́да'''|as compared to the corresponding period last year, from the same time last year}}

====Usage notes====
* Use the appropriate case of '''год''' after simple or compound numbers ending in {{m|ru|оди́н}} (1), {{m|ru|два}} (2), {{m|ru|три}} (3), or {{m|ru|четы́ре}} (4), except for 11, 12, 13 and 14 (and 111 - 114, 211 - 214 etc.) - for these and all other numbers, and with [[adverb]]s of quantity (''{{m|ru|мно́го}}'', ''{{m|ru|ско́лько}}'', etc.), use the appropriate case of {{m|ru|ле́то}}.
* After numbers that must be followed by a nominative or genitive '''singular''', the appropriate form of '''[[год]]''' is used. After numbers that must be followed by a '''genitive plural''', the form '''[[лет]]''' is used. When the number is in the dative, instrumental, or prepositional case, the appropriate form of '''[[год]]''' must be used. Examples: '''оди́н год''' (nominative singular), '''два го́да''' (genitive singular), '''три го́да''' (genitive singular), '''пять лет''' (genitive plural); but '''бо́льше трёх лет''' (genitive plural), '''бо́льше пяти́ лет''' (genitive plural); and '''пяти́ года́м''' (dative plural), '''пятью́ года́ми''' (instrumental plural), '''o пяти́ года́х''' (prepositional plural).

